| **Continuous Polyquantor** $Q_{\mathrm{poly}}^{(B)}$ | $r > 1$ | $f_\rho \ne \operatorname{id}$ | $(\;)_\rho, \mathop{\mathsf{Q}}_{f_\rho, 1}^r(A_\rho), (\;)_\rho$ |
| **Continuous Monoquantor** | $r = 1$ | $f_\rho \ne \operatorname{id}$ | $\beta_\rho \equiv f_\rho ; \alpha_\rho$ |
| **Discrete Polyquantor** $Q_{\mathrm{poly}}^{(r)}$ | $r > 1$ | $f_\rho = \operatorname{id}$ | $(\;)_\rho, \mathop{\mathsf{Q}}_{\rho, 1}^r(A_\rho), (\;)_\rho$ |
| **Monoquantor** $Q_{\mathrm{mono}}$ | $r = 1$ | $f_\rho = \operatorname{id}$ | $a, \mathsf{Q}[AS]_\gamma b$ |
| **Universalquantor ($\mathbf{U}$)** | **All $\mathfrak{A}$** | **Global Invariant** | Right Adjoint $\forall_f$ |

::: {.intuition-box .fragment}
**Theorem 1.5 & Prop. 1.6 (Polyquantor Apodiktizität):** Every polyquantor contains at least one absolutely apodictic baseline term $a_i \in \AP_0$ (SM, p. 21).
:::

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
Proposition 1.2 classifies the 2^3 - 1 = 7 nonempty aspect subsystems. Notice why any partial generator must keep the arity n fixed: if P_nn changed dimension while D_nn and K_n remained static, predicates would be left uncoordinated. Only the total subsystem {D_nn, K_n, P_nn} permits changing n.
:::

