## §1.2.1–1.2.2: The Base Category $(\Ban, \otpi)$ {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-a">STRATUM A: PURE MATHEMATICAL FOUNDATIONS (DEF. 1.6 / 1.9 &amp; SCHOLIA)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="52%"}

::: {.intuition-box}
**Intuitive Guide: A Context as a Local Scientific Laboratory**
Why model a subjective perspective as a normed Banach space? Every laboratory works with a finite array of measurement channels ($P^U$), operates within bounded saturation thresholds ($\|T\|_{\op} \le 1$), and weighs data by confidence ($D^U$).
:::

::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Definition 1.6 / 1.9: The Symmetric Monoidal Closed Category $(\Ban, \otpi)$**

1. **Objects:** Real Banach spaces $(X, \|\cdot\|_X)$.
2. **Morphisms:** Linear contractions $T \colon X \to Y$ with $\|T\|_{\op} \coloneqq \sup_{\|x\|_X \le 1} \|T(x)\|_Y \le 1$.
3. **Completed Projective Tensor Product ($X \otpi Y$):**
$$
\|u\|_{X \otpi Y} \coloneqq \inf \left\{ \sum_{i=1}^\infty \|x_i\|_X \|y_i\|_Y \;\middle|\; u = \sum_{i=1}^\infty x_i \otimes y_i,\; \sum_{i=1}^\infty \|x_i\|_X \|y_i\|_Y < \infty \right\}
$$
4. **Internal Hom Adjunction on Unit Balls:**
$$
\Hom_{\Ban}(X \otpi Y, Z) \cong \Hom_{\Ban}\big(X, \mathcal{L}(Y, Z)\big)
$$
:::

:::

::: {.column width="48%"}

::: {.carnap-box}
**Scholium 1.6 / 1.8: Why Complete the Projective Tensor Product?**
The projective cross-norm is the largest cross-norm satisfying $\|x \otimes y\|_\pi = \|x\|\,\|y\|$. It establishes an **isometric isomorphism** between bounded bilinear coordination maps $D^U \times P^U \to C^U$ and linear contractions:
$$
K^U \colon D^U \otpi P^U \longrightarrow C^U, \qquad \|K^U\|_{\op} \le 1
$$
guaranteeing that multi-channel imprinting (*Prägung*) never amplifies signal norms beyond perceptual saturation limits.
:::

::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Vector Envelopes, Cones & Isometric Ciphers (§1.2.2)**
* Interval cone $\mathcal{I}(\mathbb{R}) \coloneqq \{(a, f, b) \in \mathbb{R}^3 \mid a \le f \le b\}$ with closed convex state cylinders $\mathcal{S}_P^U \subset \operatorname{Ball}(P^U)$, $\mathcal{S}_D^U \subset \operatorname{Ball}(D^U)$.
* Isometric Ciphers:
$$
\Isom(P^U) \coloneqq \big\{ T \in \mathcal{L}(P^U, P^U) \;\big|\; \|T(x)\|_{P^U} = \|x\|_{P^U} \;\forall x \big\}
$$
On primary Euclidean charts $P_n = (\mathbb{R}^{3n}, \|\cdot\|_2)$, $\Isom(P_n) = \mathrm{O}(3n)$.
:::

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
Crossing into Stratum A, we place Heim's aspectual matrices on rigorous functional-analytic foundations. Working in the symmetric monoidal closed category Ban_<=1 with the completed projective tensor product ensures that bilinear coordination maps K^U : D^U x P^U -> C^U correspond isometrically to linear contractions on D^U tensor_pi P^U.
:::

