## §1.4: Subobject Classifier $\Omega$, Kripke–Joyal Forcing & Hyperdoctrines {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-a">STRATUM A: INTERNAL CONSTRUCTIVE LOGIC (THM. 1.13 / 1.18 &amp; PROP. 1.14 / 1.19)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Theorem 1.13 / 1.18: Complete Heyting Algebra $\Omega(U)$**
Truth values in $\Esyn$ generalize from $\{0,1\}$ to the sheaf $\Omega(U)$ of $\Jsyn$-closed sieves on $U$:
$$
\begin{aligned}
R_1 \Rightarrow_J R_2 &\coloneqq \{ f \colon V \to U \mid f^*(R_1) \subseteq f^*(R_2) \} \\
\neg_J R &\coloneqq (R \Rightarrow_J \bot) = \{ f \colon V \to U \mid f^*(R) = \emptyset \}
\end{aligned}
$$
**Constructive Non-Boolean Gap:** When a channel is unmeasured in $U$, $R \vee \neg_J R \ne \top_{\Omega(U)}$, so $U \not\Vdash \phi \vee \neg\phi$ without forcing $U \Vdash \bot$.
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Proposition 1.14 / 1.19: Slice Hyperdoctrine & Beck–Chevalley**
Every context morphism $f \colon V \to U$ induces an adjoint triple on subobjects:
$$
\exists_f \;\dashv\; f^* \;\dashv\; \forall_f
$$
Across any pullback square $W = V_1 \times_U V_2$, the **Beck–Chevalley isomorphisms** hold:
$$
\mathbf{BC}_\exists \colon g^* \exists_f \xrightarrow{\;\sim\;} \exists_{\pi_1} \pi_2^*, \qquad \mathbf{BC}_\forall \colon g^* \forall_f \xrightarrow{\;\sim\;} \forall_{\pi_1} \pi_2^*
$$
:::

::: {.intuition-box .fragment}
**Transporting Quantoren:** The right adjoint $\forall_f$ is the exact categorical realization of Heim's **Universalquantor ($\mathbf{U}$)**—allowing invariant laws to transport safely across distinct observer frames.
:::

:::

::: {.column width="50%"}

