## §1.5: Sheaf Descent, $\varepsilon$-Holoform Stability & Kochen–Specker {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-b">STRATUM B: DERIVED DESCENT THEOREMS (THMS. 1.17–1.18 / 1.22–1.24)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="47%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Definition 1.15 / 1.20 & Theorem 1.17 / 1.22: The Holoform Equalizer**
For an admissible cover $\mathcal{U} = \{\rho_i \colon V_i \to U\}_{i=1}^m$ and sheaf $\mathbf{P} \in \Esyn$:
$$
\Hol(\mathcal{U}, \mathbf{P}) \;\coloneqq\; \operatorname{Eq}\!\left( \prod_{i=1}^m \mathbf{P}(V_i) \overset{d^0}{\underset{d^1}{\rightrightarrows}} \prod_{i,j=1}^m \mathbf{P}(V_i \times_U V_j) \right)
$$
For additive presheaves $\mathbf{A}$, the **Descent Defect** is the Čech 0-coboundary:
$$
\Def_{\mathcal{U}}(s) \coloneqq d^0(s) - d^1(s) = \delta^0(s) \in \check{C}^1(\mathcal{U}, \mathbf{A})
$$
* **Exact Amalgamation ($c_{\mathrm{SHEAF}}$):** $\Def_{\mathcal{U}}(s) = 0 \iff \exists!\,\Gamma \in \mathbf{P}(U) \cong \Hol(\mathcal{U}, \mathbf{P})$ with $\rho_i^*(\Gamma) = s_i$.
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Theorem 1.18 / 1.24 ($\varepsilon$-Holoform Stability) & Carnap 1.2:**
Under partition-of-unity amalgamation $\Gamma_\sigma = \mathcal{G}_\sigma(s) \coloneqq \sum_{i=1}^m \sigma_i^*(s_i)$:
$$
\|\Def_{\mathcal{U}}(s)\|_{\check{C}^1} \le \varepsilon \implies \max_{1 \le k \le m} \|\rho_k^*(\Gamma_\sigma) - s_k\|_{\mathbf{A}(V_k)} \le \varepsilon
$$
* **Kochen–Specker Contextuality:** $\Gamma(\mathbf{1}, \underline{\Sigma}) = \emptyset$ is a non-vanishing Čech obstruction ($\check{H}^1 \ne 0$), **not** a logical contradiction ($U \Vdash \bot$).
:::

:::

::: {.column width="53%"}

<div class="interactive-panel">
  <h4>Interactive 3-Observer ε-Holoform &amp; Čech Cocycle Simulator</h4>
  <p class="widget-context-note">
