## §1.6: Typed Mereology $\mathfrak{M}_{\mathrm{asp}}$, $t$-Norms & *Aufhebung* {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-b">STRATUM B: AXIOMATIC CEM &amp; DIALECTICAL SUBLATION (THMS. 1.22–1.24 / 1.28–1.30)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Definition 1.19 / 1.25 & 1.20 / 1.26: Internal Heyting Mereology & $t$-Norm Strength**
In $\mathfrak{M}_{\mathrm{asp}}(U) \coloneqq \Sub_{\Esyn}(\mathbf{y}(U) \times (\underline{\mathsf{Pred}}_U \sqcup \underline{\mathsf{Qual}}_U))$, parthood is $A \le B$ (satisfying **MSL-M1**, **MSL-M2**, and guarded fusion $\sigma\mathcal{X} = \bigvee_{A\in\mathcal{X}} A$). Qualifier $d_r$ and predicate $f_q$ coordinate iff:
$$
\operatorname{Strength}\big((d_r, f_q), S_{\mathrm{mod}}(x)\big) \coloneqq \chi\big( (\zeta_x)_r \sigma_{dr}(v_{dr}),\; (\mathbf{z}_x)_q \sigma_{fq}(v_{fq}) \big) > \theta_{\mathrm{coord}}(x)
$$
:::

::: {.firewall-box .fragment}
**Def. 1.22 / 1.28 & Thm. 1.23 / 1.29: Tripartite Taxonomy of Antagonismen**

1. **Mereological ($\operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{mer}}$):** $\exists A, B \le S$ with $\operatorname{Incomp}_{\mathcal{E}}(A, B) \coloneqq \llbracket |\operatorname{ev}_P(A)-\operatorname{ev}_P(B)| > \theta_{\mathrm{tol}} \rrbracket = \top_{\Omega(W)}$.
2. **Descent ($\operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{desc}}$):** Non-vanishing Čech coboundary $\Def_{\mathcal{U}}(s) \ne 0$ (while overlap $\mathbf{y}W \not\cong \mathbf{0}_{\mathcal{E}}$ remains non-zero, preserving subcanonicity).
3. **Logical ($\operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{log}}$):** Internal contradiction $W \Vdash \bot$ (requires explicit translation axiom $p_{v_1} \vdash \neg p_{v_2}$).
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Theorem 1.24 / 1.30 (Reflexive Abstraction as *Aufhebung*):**
Dialectical sublation maps $S_{\mathrm{mod}}(x) \to S'_{\mathrm{mod}}(x')$ containing $C \coloneqq \operatorname{Synthesize}(A, B) \in \Prop_1$ free of internal incompatibility.
:::

:::

::: {.column width="50%"}

