Section 1.6 distinguishes three levels of Antagonismus: Mereological incompatibility, Cech Descent failure, and outright Logical Contradiction. Crucially, Descent failure does not make the overlap context W equal to the zero object, preserving subcanonicity. When an incompatibility arises, Reflexive Abstraction (Aufhebung) lifts the conflict into a higher-level syndrome C in Prop_1.
:::

