## §1.7: Pseudometric $d_P$, Metropie Flow & Lawvere–Tierney Closure {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-b">STRATUM B: LAYER 2 MODAL FRAMES &amp; STAGE I RUNNING EXAMPLE</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Def. 1.25 / 1.31 & Def. 1.27 / 1.33: Pseudometric $d_P$ & Metropie $g_{\mathrm{met}}$**
$$
d_P(U, V) \coloneqq \inf_{\alpha, \beta} \max_{F \in \{D,P,C\}} \max\!\big( \|I_{F^U} - \beta_F \alpha_F\|_{\op},\; \|I_{F^V} - \alpha_F \beta_F\|_{\op} \big)
$$
Along smooth cipher paths $\gamma(t) = z(t) \in \mathrm{SO}(n)$, the **Infinitesimal Metropie Tensor** is:
$$
g_{\mathrm{met}}(\dot{z}_1, \dot{z}_2) \coloneqq -\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}\!\big((z^{-1}\dot{z}_1)(z^{-1}\dot{z}_2)\big) \ge 0, \quad d_{\mathbf{Ctx}}(U,V) \le \inf_\gamma \int_0^1 \sqrt{g_{\mathrm{met}}(\dot{\gamma},\dot{\gamma})}\,dt
$$
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Theorems 1.29–1.30 / 1.37–1.38: Lawvere–Tierney Modal Bridge & Plus-Construction**
On Fischer–Servi frames satisfying Metric Confluence ($A_{\mathrm{conf}}$: FS1 & FS2 on $d_P(U_1, U_2) < \epsilon_A$), $\Diamond_S \dashv \Box_S$ form an internal Galois adjunction on $\Omega$, and $j_S \coloneqq \neg_J \Box_S \neg_J \colon \Omega \to \Omega$ is a **Lawvere–Tierney topology** whose sheafification is the two-step plus-construction:
$$
(L_{j_S} P)(U) = \operatorname*{colim}_{S \in J_{j_S}(U)} \operatorname{Nat}(S, P), \qquad \mathbf{a}_{j_S} P = L_{j_S}(L_{j_S} P) \;\dashv\; \mathbf{i}_{j_S}
$$
:::

:::

::: {.column width="50%"}

