## §1.9: Soundness, Completeness & Lean 4 Verification {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-b">STRATUM B: HENKIN COMPLETENESS, HAUPTSATZ &amp; LEAN 4 BLUEPRINT</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Theorems 1.34, 1.37–1.38 / 1.42, 1.45–1.46: Soundness & Strong Completeness**
By simultaneous multi-level prime theory saturation $\mathbf{\Delta} = \langle \Delta_k \subset \mathcal{L}_k \rangle_{k \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ over canonical worlds $w^c = (\Delta_k, k)$ with $(\Delta_k, k) R_{\pi_F}^c (\Delta_{k+1}, k+1)$:
$$
(\Delta_k, k) \models \psi \;\Longleftrightarrow\; \psi \in \Delta_k \quad \forall \psi \in \mathcal{L}_k
$$
Therefore, syntactic derivability and leveled Kripke validity coincide across all strata:
$$
\boxed{S(x);\; \Gamma_G \vdash^k \phi \;\Longleftrightarrow\; S(x);\; \Gamma_G \models^k \phi}
$$
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Gentzen's *Hauptsatz* & Structural Metatheorems (Appendix A)**

* **Cut Elimination (Thm A.5):** Every derivable sequent admits a cut-free derivation $\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{norm}}$.
* **Subformula Property (Thm A.6) & Disjunction Property (Thm A.8):** $S(x);\emptyset \vdash^k \phi_1 \vee \phi_2 \implies S(x);\emptyset \vdash^k \phi_1$ or $S(x);\emptyset \vdash^k \phi_2$.
* **Absolute Syntactic Consistency (Cor A.7):** $S(x); \emptyset \nvdash^k \bot$.
:::

:::

::: {.column width="50%"}
### Compile-Ready Lean 4 Blueprint (`StratumA.Topos`, App. C)

<div class="lean-code-card">
<pre style="margin:0;"><code>import Mathlib
open CategoryTheory
namespace Syntrometrie.StratumA.Topos

structure StructuredContext where
  D : Type
  P : Type
  C : Type
  [instD : NormedAddCommGroup D] [instDSpace : NormedSpace ℝ D] [instDFin : FiniteDimensional ℝ D]
  [instP : NormedAddCommGroup P] [instPSpace : NormedSpace ℝ P] [instPFin : FiniteDimensional ℝ P]
  [instC : NormedAddCommGroup C] [instCSpace : NormedSpace ℝ C] [instCFin : FiniteDimensional ℝ C]
  K : D →L[ℝ] (P →L[ℝ] C)
  K_contractive : ‖K‖ ≤ 1
  z : P ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] P
  zeta : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] D

lemma opNorm_comp_le_one {E F G : Type*}
    [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F]
    [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℝ G]
    (f : E →L[ℝ] F) (g : F →L[ℝ] G) (hf : ‖f‖ ≤ 1) (hg : ‖g‖ ≤ 1) :
    ‖g.comp f‖ ≤ 1 := by
  calc ‖g.comp f‖ ≤ ‖g‖ * ‖f‖ := ContinuousLinearMap.opNorm_comp_le g f
    _ ≤ 1 * 1 := mul_le_mul hg hf (norm_nonneg f) zero_le_one
    _ = 1 := mul_one 1</code></pre>
</div>

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
Section 1.9 and Appendix A establish the crown jewels of our proof theory: Soundness, Strong Canonical Completeness via multi-level prime theory saturation, and Gentzen's Hauptsatz (Cut-Elimination), which guarantees absolute syntactic consistency. On the right is the Mathlib-checked Lean 4 formalization of StructuredContext and operator norm contractivity.
:::

