## §1.10–1.11: Reconstruction Map $\mathcal{R}$ & Chapter 1 Synthesis {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-c">STRATUM C: CARNAP 1.3, MASTER REGISTER (SM EQS. 1–4) &amp; BRIDGE TO CH. 2</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="54%"}

| Heimian Concept ($\mathbf{D}$) | Mathematical Explicatum ($\mathcal{R}$ in $\mathbf{A}/\mathbf{B}$) | Status & Ref. |
|:---|:---|:---:|
| **Subjektiver Aspekt ($S$, Eq. 1)** | Context $U = (D, P, C, K, z, \zeta, \mathcal{S}_D, \mathcal{S}_P) \in \Ctx$ | **A-Def** (§1.2.3) |
| **Prädikatband $[a, f, b]_q$** | Convex interval cylinder $\mathcal{S}_P^U \subset \operatorname{Ball}(P^U)$ | **A-Def** (§1.2.2) |
| **Basischiffren ($z_n, \zeta_n$)** | Linear isometries in $\Isom(P^U), \Isom(D^U)$ | **A-Def** (§1.2.2) |
| **Koordination ($K_n$)** | Projective contraction $K^U \colon D^U \otpi P^U \to C^U$ | **A-Def** (§1.2.1) |
| **Metropie ($g$)** | Pseudometric $d_P(U,V)$ & trace tensor $g_{\mathrm{met}}$ | **B-Model** (§1.7) |
| **Mono-/Polyquantor (Eqs. 2–4)** | Local $U \Vdash \phi$ & product forcing $\prod_{i=1}^r V_i \Vdash \phi$ | **A-Def** (§1.4) |
| **Universalquantor ($\mathbf{U}$)** | Right-adjoint dependent product $\forall_f$ ($f^* \dashv \forall_f$) | **A-Prop** (§1.4) |
| **Holoform ($\mathbf{H}$)** | Global section $\Gamma \in \Hol(\mathcal{U}, \mathbf{P})$ ($\Def_{\mathcal{U}}(s) = 0$) | **B-Thm** (§1.5) |
| **Antagonismus** | Tripartite obstruction ($\operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{mer}}, \operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{desc}}, \operatorname{Ant}_{\mathrm{log}}$) | **B-Thm** (§1.6) |

::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Asymptotic Sanity Check (Classical Boolean Collapse):**
When $\Ctx \to \{*\}$, $z = \zeta = \operatorname{id}$, and $a_q = f_q = b_q$, the sheaf topos collapses to $\mathbf{Sh}(\{*\}) \cong \mathbf{Set}$ and $\Omega \cong \{0, 1\} = \mathbf{2}$, recovering classical bivalent Tarskian semantics as an uncontextualized degenerate limit.
:::

:::

::: {.column width="46%"}

::: {.carnap-box}
**Carnap 1.3: $\mathcal{R}$ as Scientific Representation (van Fraassen 2008)**
$\mathcal{R} \colon \mathsf{HeimVocabulary}\;(\mathbf{D}) \rightsquigarrow \mathsf{MathStructures}\;(\mathbf{A}, \mathbf{B})$ satisfies Carnap's four explication criteria (**Similarity**, **Exactness**, **Fruitfulness**, **Simplicity**) while strictly respecting the Epistemic Firewall.
:::

